{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1146216-an-elegant-solution","id":1146216,"title":"An elegant solution","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-02T19:10:33-07:00","id":1146216,"title":"An elegant solution","content":"I was in a discussion yesterday with my Changeling DM. The nature of the discussion was about the Goblin Market. He wanted to add that getting a Merit or Contract from the Market would force a degeneration check.<br /> <br /> He was unhappy with the rules on goblin market in which the Market serves as the meta-excuse on how the character gets merits/contracts by expending XP. Basically the &quot;coin&quot; the changeling use to buy stuff is XP and he get his merits/contracts and no question asked.<br /> <br /> Personally i am happy with it. I have learned that if the book doesnt say the powers cost anything to get them beyond XP, then spend XP and no question asked (Wolf Gifts, a good example). Putting a cost (like clarity) is just yet another paperwork the player has to hurdle to get what it wants and it generates a sense of resentment from the players as he might feel cheated with the DM changing the rules against him for no other reason that &quot;because is more dramatic that way&quot;.<br /> <br /> He however insisted on he wanted that belonging to a Court mattered more. That buying things on the goblin market robs is free no-string-attached way for PCs to get stuff and that made the importance of Courts lesser. He wanted to create a situation in which either the players choose the court option with the strings attached or else risk a degeneration check but with no strings-attached.<br /> <br /> Where i am going with this? I am recently finding time to get up to date with Requiem. Reading all the books again and reading 2nd editions (i am full of questions) but i wanted to point out something i notice after the aforementioned discussion.<br /> <br /> Requiem 2nd approached the issue i mentioned and solve it in such a elegant way that i feel the need to point it out for kudos. The way it approach it was as a series of cheap Merits (1 or 2 dots) that give your punctuation of the Status in the organization into merits points for free in other merits. To represent the perks of an organization.<br /> <br /> The way this is good is because it allows both types of character to exist. You can have the lone wolf that buys his merits and never compromise, his merits are gonna be protected by sanctity of merits. <br /> <br /> On the other hand the joiner gets a bunch of free merits that he will have never to pay for and if dependent on him belonging to the organization.<br /> <br /> <br /> So that, kudos to Requiem for handling something so well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}